  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from Total Governmental Funds column (p4): 62,223,228 + 41,715,380 - 46,797,906 + 15,314,573 - 10,879,472 + other financing 3,360,264 (insurance recoveries 3,409,093, leases terminated -48,829) = 64,936,067 reconciles. Business-type from proprietary Total enterprise column (p6; internal service funds excluded): 219,106,094 + 94,738,194 - 77,235,467 - 4,435,101 + 826,607 (net contributed capital 1,018,228, loss on sale -191,621) = 233,000,327; no single printed receipts/disbursements total, so operating + nonoperating revenue/expense lines were added. Transfers: governmental net +4,435,101 = business-type net -4,435,101. ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash 43,346,628 + county treasurer cash 202,055; investments 26,025,098 separate. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column; interfund receivable/payable line nets to '-' in the Total column and is omitted. Detail: General, Street and Sales Tax budget schedules (pp9-11; budgetary basis, e.g. General property 6,113,565 vs GAAP 6,104,270); nonmajor combining statement (pp12-13) has 14 fund columns so its Total column is used as 'Nonmajor funds (combined)'. 'Business' tax line kept as occupation/franchise tax (review). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
